  a fake and run under plain Node. That's a small piece of indirection existing purely for testability, and it's the
  same seam a server-backed store would use.

  [1mThe honest gap:[0m [38;5;153mrender.js[39m and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m get no automated coverage. Verifying that the badge actually appears in the DOM
  needs a browser, which is what end-to-end tests would have given us. That's the accepted cost of unit-tests-only —
  worth naming now rather than discovering later.
